{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-09-Nov-2022-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Two trains - A and B- having the lengths 195 m and 165 m, respectively, are running in the same direction on parallel lines. If the speed of A and B be 77 km/h and 85 km/h, respectively, what will be the time (in seconds) taken by them to cross each other?", "options": [{"text": "162", "added": false}, {"text": "164", "added": false}, {"text": "160", "added": false}, {"text": "166", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "140", "added": false}, {"text": "70", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "120", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "A field is in the shape of a rectangle of length 90 m and breadth 75 m. In one corner of the field, a pit, which is 18 m long 15 m broad and 6 m deep, has been dug out. The earth taken out of it is evenly spread over the remaining part of the field. Find the rise in the level of the field?", "options": [{"text": "27 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "25 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "28 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "24 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "A seller uses faulty weight in place of a 2 kg weight and earns a 25% profit. He claims that he is selling on the cost price in front of the customers but uses a faulty weight. How much error is there in the 2 kg weight to gain 25%?", "options": [{"text": "250 g", "added": false}, {"text": "400 g", "added": false}, {"text": "500 g", "added": false}, {"text": "300 g", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3r", "added": false}, {"text": "2r", "added": false}, {"text": "πr2", "added": false}, {"text": "r2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "The angles of a triangle are in the ratio 1 : 1 : 2. What percentage of the total internal angle is the greatest angle?", "options": [{"text": "50%", "added": false}, {"text": "65%", "added": false}, {"text": "45%", "added": false}, {"text": "40%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "The average salary of all the employees in a company is Rs.14,000. The average salary of 5 technicians is Rs.18,000 and the average salary of the rest is Rs.13,200. The total number of employees in the company is:", "options": [{"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "29", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "A faulty weighing machine reads 1 kg when 900 gm is actually weighted on it. The shopkeeper marked the price of his goods by 10%, but unfortunately he was caught by the metrology department and then they ordered him to repair his weighing machine and gave punishment to sell the goods at 10% discount on cost price for a month. If each customer is now paying ₹20 for 1 kg, then before the raid _______ amount they have paid for the same quantity. (Rounded off to two places of decimal)", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "∆ABC and ∆DEF are two triangles such that ∆ABC ≅ ∆FDE. If AB = 5 cm, ∠B = 40° and ∠A = 80°, then which of the following options is true?", "options": [{"text": "DF = 5 cm, ∠E = 60°", "added": false}, {"text": "DE = 5 cm, ∠F = 60°", "added": false}, {"text": "DE = 5 cm, ∠D = 60°", "added": false}, {"text": "DE = 5 cm, ∠E = 60°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "Viraj, Vishal, Mohit", "added": false}, {"text": "Vishal, Viraj, Viraj", "added": false}, {"text": "Shivam, Viraj, Vishal", "added": false}, {"text": "Mohit, Viraj, Vishal", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "To do a certain task X would take 3 times as long as Y and Z together; and Z would takes 4 times as long as Y and X together. Three of them together can complete the task in 10 days. How much time is taken by X and Z to complete the task?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "On a certain sum, the difference between compound interest and simple interest at 10% per annum for 2 years is Rs.250. The sum is _________.", "options": [{"text": "Rs.25,450", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.26,550", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.25,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.26,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "si-ci-difference", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "Which of the following is a prime number?", "options": [{"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "39", "added": false}, {"text": "68", "added": false}, {"text": "89", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "types-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "In an election between 2 parties A and B, A gets 37% of total votes cast and thus lost by 338 votes. The total number of casted votes is (assume none of the votes was declared invalid):", "options": [{"text": "1300", "added": false}, {"text": "1500", "added": false}, {"text": "1200", "added": false}, {"text": "1800", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "15,00,000 tonnes", "added": false}, {"text": "1,00,000 tonnes", "added": false}, {"text": "10,000 tonnes", "added": false}, {"text": "10,00,000 tonnes", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "The least common multiple of a and b is 42. The LCM of 5a and 11b is :", "options": [{"text": "2310", "added": false}, {"text": "4620", "added": false}, {"text": "210", "added": false}, {"text": "462", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "A thief is spotted by a policeman from a distance of 250m. When the policeman starts the chase, the thief also starts running. Assuming that the speed of the thief is 10 km/h and that of the policeman is 12 km/h, how far would the thief have run before he is caught?", "options": [{"text": "4 km", "added": false}, {"text": "1.25 km", "added": false}, {"text": "3 km", "added": false}, {"text": "2 km", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "If 25 persons can complete a work in 140 days, then how many persons will be required to complete the same work in 70 days?", "options": [{"text": "70", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "If p : q = 4 : 5, q : r = 3 : 4 and r : s = 2 : 5, then p : s is:", "options": [{"text": "2 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "6 : 25", "added": false}, {"text": "5 : 2", "added": false}, {"text": "25 : 6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "Four numbers are in the ratio 1 : 2 : 3 : 5. Two times their sum is 44. Find the ratio in the numbers obtained by subtracting 3 from the cube of each number.", "options": [{"text": "2 : 31 : 204 : 999", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 13 : 208 : 992", "added": false}, {"text": "11 : 67 : 219 : 1003", "added": false}, {"text": "5 : 61 : 213 : 997", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "On a straight road, a bus is 30 km ahead of a car travelling in the same direction. After 3 hours, the car is 60 km ahead of the bus. If the speed of the bus is 42 km/h, then find the speed of the car.", "options": [{"text": "67 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "72 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "65 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "59 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "What is the least value of x so that the number 8x5215 becomes divisible by 9?", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "Find the perimeter of major sector of a circle of radius 12 metres, whose minor sector subtends an angle of 75° at the centre.", "options": [{"text": "24 + 5π metres", "added": false}, {"text": "24 + 19π metres", "added": false}, {"text": "24 – 5π metres", "added": false}, {"text": "24 – 19π metres", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "205", "added": false}, {"text": "214", "added": false}, {"text": "185", "added": false}, {"text": "198", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "Y and Z", "added": false}, {"text": "Y", "added": false}, {"text": "X and Y", "added": false}, {"text": "X and Z", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "65.5", "added": false}, {"text": "63.8", "added": false}, {"text": "60.5", "added": false}, {"text": "58.2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "76.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "80.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "82.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "85.5%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "roots", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "A number, when divided by 15 and 18 every time, leaves 3 as a remainder, the least possible number is:", "options": [{"text": "83", "added": false}, {"text": "103", "added": false}, {"text": "39", "added": false}, {"text": "93", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "79.33", "added": false}, {"text": "77.67", "added": false}, {"text": "82.66", "added": false}, {"text": "73", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "A mixer marked at Rs.2,300 is sold for Rs.2,024. What is the percentage of discount?", "options": [{"text": "13%", "added": false}, {"text": "10%", "added": false}, {"text": "12%", "added": false}, {"text": "11%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "45.48 percent", "added": false}, {"text": "35.48 percent", "added": false}, {"text": "34.25 percent", "added": false}, {"text": "39.18 percent", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "75 unit2", "added": false}, {"text": "70 unit2", "added": false}, {"text": "60 unit2", "added": false}, {"text": "50 unit2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 40, "text": "The ratio between the height and radius of the base of a cylinder is 7 : 5. If its volume is 14836.5 cm3, then find its total surface area (take π = 3.14).", "options": [{"text": "3391.2 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "5391.2 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "4391.2 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "5591.2 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 41, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "39,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "32,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "36,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "21,00,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 42, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2016", "added": false}, {"text": "2020", "added": false}, {"text": "2019", "added": false}, {"text": "2017", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 43, "text": "A tradesman marks his goods at 26% above the cost price. He allows his customer a discount of 12% on the marked price. His profit per cent is:", "options": [{"text": "10.88%", "added": false}, {"text": "11.08%", "added": false}, {"text": "10.50%", "added": false}, {"text": "10%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 44, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 45, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0.5", "added": false}, {"text": "−1", "added": false}, {"text": "−0.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 46, "text": "In ΔABC, DE ∥ BC in such a way that A-D-B and A-E-C. If m⎿ ACB = 40°, then m⎿ DAE + m⎿ ADE =_________.", "options": [{"text": "240°", "added": false}, {"text": "120°", "added": false}, {"text": "140°", "added": false}, {"text": "230°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 47, "text": "What is the volume of a cube whose surface area is 54 cm2?", "options": [{"text": "28 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "3 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "27 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "9 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 48, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 49, "text": "The cost of two varieties of tea is ₹300 and ₹375 respectively. If both the varieties of tea are mixed together in the ratio 3 : 2, then what should be the price of mixed variety of tea per kg?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 50, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}]}